From: "lich.wang" <lich.wang@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:07:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: sequencing: qcom-wcn: reset the TB710FU WCN7850 on
 WLAN enable

The bootloader leaves the WCN7850 powered with its 48 MHz reference
clock off, so its ROM sits in EDL and MHI never reaches READY.  Hold the
enable low for a full PMU power cycle (2 ms is not enough) before
raising it.

From MeteoricmeteorLL/tb710fu-linux.
---
 drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
index e754dc7e8..5d1821978 100644
--- a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
+++ b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
@@ -379,6 +379,16 @@ static int pwrseq_qcom_wcn_wlan_enable(struct pwrseq_device *pwrseq)
 	struct pwrseq_qcom_wcn_ctx *ctx = pwrseq_device_get_drvdata(pwrseq);
 
 	pwrseq_qcom_wcn_ensure_gpio_delay(ctx);
+	/*
+	 * TB710FU: the bootloader leaves the WCN7850 powered with its 48 MHz
+	 * reference clock off, so its ROM sits in EDL and MHI never reaches
+	 * READY.  Hold the enable low long enough for a full PMU power cycle
+	 * (2 ms is not enough) to give the ROM a real reset edge.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,tb710fu")) {
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ctx->wlan_gpio, 0);
+		msleep(100);
+	}
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ctx->wlan_gpio, 1);
 	ctx->last_gpio_enable_jf = jiffies;
 
